{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Silver</b> — Like silver: the words of the discerning are accounted as choice, refined silver." "<b>Like little</b> — Learned from them a little." "Another interpretation: <b>Heart</b> — its meaning is knowledge; the meaning of 'their knowledge is like little' is that it is choice, the opposite of the tongue of the righteous."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "The phrase 'the opposite of the tongue of the righteous' is cryptic in the Hebrew; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:00.513796887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}